        }
      ],
      "content": "A stone (probably building or paving stone) named for Hasborough — the same toponym (Hazebrouck, Flanders) that gives the cloth its name (cf. Willan 35). Distinct from the Hazebrouck cloth, whose spellings are now folded into the `cloth` entry as a locational qualifier. Compare `caen stone`. Precise identification uncertain."
    }
